  "title": "how much the layered layout should know about a drawn group, re-asked after two review rounds",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "Q6 of docs/plans/groups-in-the-layout/PLAN.md — the Q2 fork re-opened, with the cost each side has actually accumulated",
  "explanation": "Q2 chose [keeping a group as one box](#as-one-unit) because it reused the pass that already works. Two review rounds have added five modifications to that pass, plus a third pass whose only job is letting the outside reorder a group's members — which is the defining property of [the option Q2 rejected](#one-constrained-pass). Every one of those additions exists because a group became a box of a size nothing else has; under the rejected option every box stays the size it is today and none of them is needed. What the rejected option costs has not changed and has not been measured: the crossing sweeps and the column packing both have to learn the rule. Leaves out everything the two options agree on, which is most of the plan.",
